# AI-only development

The human does **not** write or edit project code. Every code change, fix, refactor, test, and config edit must be performed by the agent.

## Agent owns

- Source, tests, assets, CI, Cursor rules/skills/commands
- Running tooling (`melos`, `flutter`, `dart`, `build_runner`, lints, tests)
- Commits and PRs when the human asks
- Investigating failures and applying fixes

## Human owns (non-code only)

- Product decisions and approvals
- Manual device / UI verification
- Secrets, store/dashboard logins, and 2FA the agent cannot access
- Saying what to build next

## Hard rules

- Never ask the human to edit files, paste patches, or "run this change yourself".
- Never leave unfinished implementation with "you can add X later" — implement it or ask a product question.
- If blocked on a human-only action, say exactly what they must do (one short step), then continue everything else yourself.
- Prefer doing the work over explaining how the human would do it.
- After changes, verify with the project's usual checks when reasonable; report what you ran and what still needs human device testing.
